# netsurf: Vita http and https through libcurl on mbedTLS (frontends/vita)
# Generated 2026-09-23
#
# Phase 1's networking item: pages from the web, not only app0:.
# - Makefile.defaults: NETSURF_USE_CURL=YES with vdpm's curl-mbedtls
#   (libcurl 8.22, mbedTLS 3.6.5 LTS: TLS 1.3); OpenSSL stays off (NetSurf's
#   OpenSSL hooks are optional; the Vita's OpenSSL package is 1.0.2).
# - Makefile: net.c; -lpthread (mbedTLS is built with pthread threading).
# - net.c/.h (new): sceNet start-up, once, for curl and the diagnostics
#   mirror alike (it was inside netlog.c, so netlog.cfg "off" would have
#   left curl without a network); 1 MiB sceNet pool.
# - netlog.c: uses net.c.
# - main.c: ca_bundle defaults to app0:/res/ca-bundle.pem (Mozilla's roots,
#   bundled by the VitaBrowser repo) instead of the firmware's 2017 list;
#   network pages after the bundled ones (defaults: example.com over http
#   and https; ux0:data/VitaBrowser/nettest.txt overrides), reached by L/R
#   and by a new autotest pass N that times and dumps them, kept apart
#   from the timing passes A-D. mbedTLS's entropy is newlib's getentropy()
#   -> sceKernelGetRandomNumber (vitaSDK's mbedtls.patch).
# See docs/phase-0/10-hardware-test-plan.md §Run 8.

